  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 4857918aa396e664da4bf6e1e0405844, type: 3}
  m_Name: Level1(1-4)
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  dialogue:
  - "\"Is there anything that stands out to you from what you\u2019ve read...?\""
  - "I don\u2019t like when there are exaggerated stereotypes, or outdated ideas.
    \r\nBut maybe because the earlier materials have flaws like this, it feels better
    to see how the characters change over time, in publications years down the line.
    \n"
  - "Though it is pretty annoying that there isn\u2019t a lot of reading material
    besides the informative stuff, like summaries and wiki pages. "
  - "Maybe most characters from the late 1930s are too overshadowed by the more famous
    series that were created around then. So no one really cared about them for a
    long time. \r\n"
  - "But even if they weren\u2019t popular for a while, people still notice and remember
    them later, and that\u2019s why the museum exists!\r\n"
  responses: []
